WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.669
-Today, Donald Trump became
the third President

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:04.904
in history
to be impeached.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:07.173
For more on this it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:11.244
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.912
Well, here we are.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.414
President Trump
has been impeached.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:15.915
You know.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.084
The serial racist criminal who's
already cheated in one election,

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.486
obstructed justice in the
investigation of that election,

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:23.289
used his office to enrich
himself, solicited bribes,

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.624
inflicted human rights abuses
on migrant families,

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:27.226
been accused
of sexual assault,

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:29.495
had six close associates
indicted or jailed,

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:30.597
you remember that guy?

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.064
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:34.533
No, you know, the guy who almost
definitely committed tax fraud,

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.903
admitted he broke the law
by misusing his personal charity

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.671
to help his campaign,
began his presidency

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.174
by settling a fraud lawsuit
over his scam university,

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.909
orchestrated an extortion scheme
to cheat in the 2020 election,

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:46.245
tried to cover it up,
got caught, obstructed Congress,

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:47.380
directed an illegal scheme

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.081
to pay hush money
to cover up an affair,

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.583
and drove his golf cart
onto the green.

00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:52.885
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:55.454
Yeah, that guy.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:58.258
And yet, Republicans are still
pretending to be surprised

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.526
that there are people who take
issue with President Trump.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.395
This is like one of those
news stories

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.763
where a guy gets arrested
for being

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.464
a serial killer
for 40 years

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.434
and reporters go
to his neighbors and ask,

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:10.069
"Did you suspect anything,"
and they say, "Well, one time,

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.038
I saw him with a chainsaw
wearing a hockey mask,

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:13.873
but I just assumed
he was a lumberjack

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.308
who played in the NHL."

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.677
[ Laughter ]
Now as we tape this,

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.712
we're expecting
the actual final vote

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.614
to impeach Donald Trump
to happen any minute now.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.050
I mean, like,
right after we tape this

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.285
and because we're taping
right before the vote,

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:28.588
that means we don't have
video of the actual

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:29.923
moment Trump was impeached.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.191
So as a placeholder,
we'd like to show you

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.627
the second most embarrassing
thing to happen to Donald Trump,

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.262
this clip of him
getting on Air Force One

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.831
with toilet paper
stuck to his shoe.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:41.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:44.904
Because much like
the toilet paper,

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.973
impeachment will follow Trump
wherever he goes.

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:49.442
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.245
In fact, I hope they put the
toilet paper in the Smithsonian

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.913
next to the articles
of impeachment.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.347
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:57.916
Now, after a series
of procedural votes

00:01:57.916 --> 00:02:00.453
in the House this morning,
there were hours of debate

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.521
on the actual articles
themselves.

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:05.658
And to give you an idea of the
contrast between the two sides,

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:08.728
here's a sampling of some of
the pro-impeachment speeches

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.029
during the floor debate.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:13.132
-It is tragic that
the President's reckless actions

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.234
make impeachment necessary.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.469
He gave us no choice.

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:18.838
-President Trump
has demonstrated

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.473
a clear pattern of wrongdoing.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.509
-No one in America could do
what Donald Trump did

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:24.677
and get away with it.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.979
-And it is our duty
to impeach him.

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:29.482
-No President may cheat
the people

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:33.185
by working with foreign
governments to steal from us,

00:02:33.185 --> 00:02:35.355
a free and fair election.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:38.023
-He solicited foreign
interference before,

00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:41.193
he is doing it now,
and he will do it again.

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:44.063
The President
is the smoking gun.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.465
-It's true. Trump broke the law
in plain sight

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:48.234
and admitted it.
He is the smoking gun.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.703
It's like if the cop showed up
to the crime scene

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.172
and there was Trump holding
a gun with his name on it

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:56.676
and a piece of toilet paper on
the ground with his shoe print.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.844
[ Laughter ]
Now, compare to those speeches

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:01.014
presenting evidence
of Trump's impeachable offenses

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.282
to the whiny rambling
of the Republicans.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.184
-I strongly oppose the articles
before us today

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:08.654
and I hope that we will finally
move past this nightmare!

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.990
-The matter before the House
today is based solely

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.826
on a fundamental hatred
of our President.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.729
It's a sham, a witch hunt,
and it's tantamount to a coup.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.364
He's rebuilding our military,

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.199
he helped create
the space force.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.767
-We tied up
the Intelligence Committee,

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.335
we tied up
the Judiciary Committee,

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:24.737
and, oh, by the way,
the Ways

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.472
and Means committee
had to give up their room.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:29.108
They couldn't even meet while
you were doing all of this.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:32.579
-They want to take away my vote
and throw it in the trash.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.880
They want to
take away my President.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:39.418
-I believe the Democrats are
tearing this country apart.

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.621
They're tearing families apart.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:44.824
-First of all, it is rich
to accuse Democrats

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:47.026
of tearing families apart
to defend a president

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:50.462
who is literally
tearing families apart.

00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:51.997
Second --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:54.601
Second, they all sound

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.835
like bratty teens
yelling at their parents.

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:59.239
Stop coming in my room, you're
tearing this family apart,

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.541
I have to build
my Lego space force!

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.976
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:05.044
So the House passed two articles
of impeachment against Trump.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:08.047
And if you ask me,
he got off easy with only two.

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:10.416
Remember that dumb press
conference Trump did

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.318
before he was inaugurated
where he lied

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.420
and said he'd hand off
control of his businesses

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.855
to his weird gargoyle sons

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:18.557
and stood next to stacks of
folders full of business

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.126
documents
that turned out to be blank,

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:22.761
and then, for some reason,
just wandered off the stage

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:24.797
like a confused old man?

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:25.898
Democrats should have done

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.667
that but with articles
of impeachment.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.435
This folder is for
soliciting bribes,

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.303
this folder
for human rights abuses.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:32.771
And this folder is for the way

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:35.041
Trump stands with his chest
puffed out,

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.777
you know, like he's trying
to get his hoverboard

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.212
To go forward.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.513
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.981
Looks like he's
waiting for someone

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:44.650
to throw bird seed on the ground
so he can peck at it.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.286
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:47.987
So Trump is now
the third President

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.188
in history to be impeached.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.723
Now obviously, he'll very likely
be acquitted

00:04:51.723 --> 00:04:52.858
by the Republican Senate.

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:54.793
But still, this judgment
will follow his name

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:56.429
in history forever.
And as we all know,

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:59.265
there's nothing Donald Trump
cares about more than his name.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.066
He puts it on everything
from his tower

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:03.001
to his helicopter
to his private jet.

00:05:03.001 --> 00:05:05.304
They're going to have to change
the name from Trump

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.573
to "Impeachment Airlines."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.275
Okay, folks,
we're going to fly you

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.609
about halfway
to your destination,

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:12.612
and then, another airline
will have to take you

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:14.947
the rest of the way.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.515
In fact, Trump cares so much

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:18.884
about protecting his name
and his place in history,

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:20.586
which will be permanently
marred by impeachment,

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:23.088
that yesterday, he sent
what can only be described

00:05:23.088 --> 00:05:25.190
as a truly
deranged six-page letter

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:27.527
to House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
whining about impeachment.

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:29.962
Before we get into the worst
parts of the letter,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.197
just listen to how it starts.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.332
This is the first line --
"Dear Madam Speaker,

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.868
I write to express my strongest
and most powerful protest

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.636
against the partisan
impeachment crusade."

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:39.138
Alright, first of all,
we've already seen

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:41.140
your strongest
and most powerful protest.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.908
All those times
in the Oval Office

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:44.276
where you scream
like a lunatic.

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:45.511
I mean, look at it.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.745
Looks like
something your tour guide

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:48.547
would tell you to stay away from
during a boat ride

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:49.982
through the Amazon River.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.484
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.052
But Trump's letter
just gets crazier.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:55.821
Here's just a sampling of
some of the most bat[bleep]

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:57.523
lines from this
official document

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:59.024
on White House letterhead.

00:05:59.024 --> 00:06:03.262
And just for fun, I'm going to
read it like a cartoon villain.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:04.864
"You have cheapened
the importance

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:07.133
of the very ugly
word impeachment.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:10.636
You are declaring open war
on American democracy.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.338
It is a terrible thing
you are doing,

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:14.574
but you will have
to live with it, not I."

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:15.707
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.707 --> 00:06:17.176
"You have developed
a full-fledged case

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.311
of what many in the media
call Trump derangement

00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:21.714
and sadly,
you will never get over it.

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:24.684
You are the ones bringing pain
and suffering to our republic

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:27.953
for your own selfish personal,
political and partisan gain.

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:30.956
Once the phone call was made
public, your whole plot blew up,

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:32.658
but that didn't stop you
from continuing,

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.393
and now,
I will twirl my mustache

00:06:34.393 --> 00:06:36.529
while I tie you
to these railroad tracks."

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:37.996
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.996 --> 00:06:40.800
But my favorite line from
Trump's insane letter is this.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.301
"Since the moment I won
the election,

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.970
the Democratic Party has been
possessed by impeachment fever.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:48.774
Impeachment fever sounds like
he's narrating an old newsreel

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:51.310
about the Beatles landing
in America.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.245
Impeachment fever
is sweeping the nation.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:55.314
Look at the throngs
of teenagers

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:57.249
screaming as they greet
the Fab Four.

00:06:57.249 --> 00:07:00.052
Pelosi, Schumer, Schiff,

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.820
and don't forget
the dumb one, Donald.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.856
Uh-oh, looks like
he's having trouble

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:05.725
with his umbrella again.

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.893
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:11.830
But I think maybe
the most insane line

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:12.999
from Trump's letter was this.

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:15.401
"More due process was afforded
to those accused

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:17.036
in the Salem
witch trials."

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:19.171
That's right -- Trump compared

00:07:19.171 --> 00:07:20.873
impeachment to the Salem
witch trials.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:22.307
But hey, you know.

00:07:22.307 --> 00:07:24.210
At least they didn't compare it
to the Bible.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.344
I mean, that would be insane.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:27.513
Even Republicans aren't
deranged enough

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:29.181
to compare Trump to Jesus.

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:31.316
-I want you to keep this
in mind.

00:07:31.316 --> 00:07:35.220
When Jesus was falsely accused
of treason, Pontius Pilate gave

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.691
Jesus the opportunity
to face his accusers.

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:40.292
During that sham trial,

00:07:40.292 --> 00:07:42.662
Pontius Pilate afforded
more rights to Jesus

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:44.163
than the Democrats
have afforded this

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.699
President in this process.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:47.933
-Jesus.

00:07:47.933 --> 00:07:49.935
[ Laughter ]
I mean --

00:07:49.935 --> 00:07:53.839
I mean that literally,
they actually compared him to --

00:07:53.839 --> 00:07:55.675
These people are
out of their minds!

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:57.543
Soon, they're going to start
claiming they saw images

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:58.978
of Trump appear in their food.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:02.014
It was a miracle. I saw Trump's
face in a piece of toast.

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:03.315
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.315 --> 00:08:05.751
But Trump has also been
complaining that Democrats

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:07.386
are abusing
the impeachment process

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:08.754
as was laid out
on the Constitution.

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:11.290
And in particular, Trump has
complained multiple times

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.826
recently that impeachment
is only supposed to be used

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:16.162
sparingly
and reserved for presidents

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:18.564
who have committed
even more crimes than he has.

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:20.065
-It meant something.

00:08:20.065 --> 00:08:24.036
When you had serious
high crimes and misdemeanors.

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:27.139
When you had serious crimes --
it's impeachment.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:29.108
That would happen
every 50 years,

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:32.077
every 40 years,
every 100 years.

00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:33.212
This was a big deal.

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.747
I think it's a horrible thing

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:37.382
to be using the tool
of impeachment,

00:08:37.382 --> 00:08:39.952
which is supposed to be
used in an emergency,

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:43.656
and it would seem many,
many, many years apart.

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:46.392
-It's not supposed to be
many, many years apart.

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:49.695
Impeachment's not Halley's
Comet. It's a fire truck.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:51.964
It shows up
when there's a fire.

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:53.265
[ Laughter ]
You're not allowed to say,

00:08:53.265 --> 00:08:55.400
"We can only use that hydrant
once every 50 years.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:58.004
Sorry about your house."

00:08:58.004 --> 00:09:00.940
Trump also continued to put his
Republican supporters in a bind

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.642
by insisting that the phone call
with the president of Ukraine

00:09:03.642 --> 00:09:05.878
was not just unimpeachable
but perfect

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:08.247
and he refused to take
any responsibility at all

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:09.481
for what was
happening to him.

00:09:09.481 --> 00:09:11.851
-Mr. President, do you take
any responsibility

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:13.819
for the fact that you're
about to be impeached?

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:18.190
-No, I don't take any,
zero, to put it mildly.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.359
They took a perfect phone call

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:24.030
that I had with
the president of Ukraine,

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.764
an absolutely perfect call.

00:09:25.764 --> 00:09:27.633
You know it, they all know it,

00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:29.534
nothing was said wrong
in that call.

00:09:29.534 --> 00:09:31.837
-No, we don't know that
because it's not true.

00:09:31.837 --> 00:09:33.138
Trump's like a guy at a party

00:09:33.138 --> 00:09:34.573
telling you
an embarrassing story

00:09:34.573 --> 00:09:36.576
who assumes the same thing
has happened to you.

00:09:36.576 --> 00:09:38.243
"The other night,
I ate too much chili,

00:09:38.243 --> 00:09:41.146
got drunk, went to karaoke,
puked, slipped on the puke,

00:09:41.146 --> 00:09:42.682
farted and split my pants.

00:09:42.682 --> 00:09:44.784
You know, guys, you've been
there, we've all been there."

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:46.051
[ Laughter ]

00:09:46.051 --> 00:09:48.253
Whenever Trump does this,
he makes it impossible

00:09:48.253 --> 00:09:50.256
for even his staunchest allies
to defend him.

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:52.557
Just take GOP
Congressman Doug Collins,

00:09:52.557 --> 00:09:55.160
who was asked during
yesterday's impeachment hearing

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.029
was Trump's call perfect?

00:09:57.029 --> 00:09:59.932
And Collins, instead of
answering the simple question,

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:03.335
spewed a bunch of incoherent
nonsense until he just gave up.

00:10:03.335 --> 00:10:06.505
-Was the President's call
with President Zelensky perfect,

00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:08.139
as the President has said,

00:10:08.139 --> 00:10:12.277
and was it appropriate for him
to ask another country

00:10:12.277 --> 00:10:14.813
to investigate
an American citizen?

00:10:14.813 --> 00:10:17.249
-As I've said before, there was
nothing wrong with the call,

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:19.051
and then, when you look at it,
again, I --

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:23.656
frankly, the last --

00:10:23.656 --> 00:10:25.057
The problem I'm having right now

00:10:25.057 --> 00:10:28.227
is exactly the last
15 minutes of this.

00:10:28.227 --> 00:10:30.096
Great oratory on a lot of things

00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:32.464
that mean nothing
to this actual impeachment.

00:10:32.464 --> 00:10:36.736
I mean, get down to the bottom
line here, and -- honestly --

00:10:36.736 --> 00:10:38.404
let him answer that question,
I'm get back to it later --

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:40.773
Because everything
has been thrown out here

00:10:40.773 --> 00:10:43.341
is exactly the what the problem
we've had in the discussion,

00:10:43.341 --> 00:10:46.245
and this idea of --
we've disproven the facts,

00:10:46.245 --> 00:10:48.914
we've talked about the law,
put it in the Constitution --

00:10:48.914 --> 00:10:50.349
so I'm not --
I can yell them both,

00:10:50.349 --> 00:10:53.585
i can talk about both of them,
the problem we have here is, is,

00:10:53.585 --> 00:10:55.421
this is the very problem
we have --

00:10:55.421 --> 00:10:57.556
and I'll just address one thing
before I let it back,

00:10:57.556 --> 00:10:59.291
or if you want me
to switch right now I will.

00:10:59.291 --> 00:11:01.961
-Oh, my God,
what are you talking about?

00:11:01.961 --> 00:11:04.997
He's like the worst "Taboo"
partner in history.

00:11:04.997 --> 00:11:06.865
You know the guy
who just keeps repeating

00:11:06.865 --> 00:11:09.234
the same words really fast
like it's going to help?

00:11:09.234 --> 00:11:10.736
Okay, it's like,
"Uh, okay, you know,

00:11:10.736 --> 00:11:12.371
how when there's nothing wrong,
you know, like,

00:11:12.371 --> 00:11:14.840
how sometimes you're wrong
except it's not wrong,

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.642
so there's nothing wrong,
you know, the opposite of wrong,

00:11:16.642 --> 00:11:17.976
you did nothing wrong,
it's not wrong,

00:11:17.976 --> 00:11:19.945
there's nothing wrong."
[ Buzzer ]

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:23.816
The answer was perfect,
it was a perfect call.

00:11:23.816 --> 00:11:27.453
Like his fellow Republicans...
[ Applause ]

00:11:27.453 --> 00:11:29.988
...Collins has also
been complaining

00:11:29.988 --> 00:11:32.024
about the impeachment
process itself.

00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:35.126
During both today's hearing
and yesterday's hearing,

00:11:35.126 --> 00:11:37.963
he claimed Democrats were
rushing the impeachment vote.

00:11:37.963 --> 00:11:40.732
But he kept repeating
a bizarre analogy

00:11:40.732 --> 00:11:42.501
that was very hard to follow.

00:11:42.501 --> 00:11:44.536
-The clock and the calendar
are terrible masters.

00:11:44.536 --> 00:11:46.404
They do not care about anything

00:11:46.404 --> 00:11:49.275
except getting the time done
and the calendar fixed.

00:11:49.275 --> 00:11:51.910
They do not care about facts,
they do not care about time,

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.679
and one day, the clock
and the calendar

00:11:53.679 --> 00:11:58.117
will hang along this body
in a very detrimental way.

00:11:58.117 --> 00:12:01.853
The clock and the calendar
are terrible masters.

00:12:01.853 --> 00:12:04.890
And the majority
will own that problem today.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:06.692
Because to the clock
and the calendar,

00:12:06.692 --> 00:12:08.260
facts don't matter.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:12.197
The clock and the calendar
are terrible masters.

00:12:12.197 --> 00:12:15.434
And they lead to awful results.

00:12:15.434 --> 00:12:18.136
And yes, there will be
a day of reckoning.

00:12:18.136 --> 00:12:20.405
The calendar and the clock
will continue.

00:12:20.405 --> 00:12:23.842
And so, whatever you may gain
will be short-lived.

00:12:23.842 --> 00:12:26.011
Because the clock
and the calendar

00:12:26.011 --> 00:12:27.979
also recognize common sense.

00:12:27.979 --> 00:12:30.582
-What does that mean?
[ Laughter ]

00:12:30.582 --> 00:12:33.552
The clock and the calendar
are terrible masters,

00:12:33.552 --> 00:12:35.454
but they also
recognize common sense.

00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:37.556
That sounds like
an English translation

00:12:37.556 --> 00:12:41.126
of a German fairytale designed
to make children work harder.

00:12:41.126 --> 00:12:42.861
[ Laughter ]
It sounds like Werner Herzog

00:12:42.861 --> 00:12:45.297
narrating
one of his documentaries.

00:12:45.297 --> 00:12:47.466
Nature has two primal forces,

00:12:47.466 --> 00:12:51.536
the clock and the calendar
and they are terrible masters,

00:12:51.536 --> 00:12:53.472
but they understand
common sense,

00:12:53.472 --> 00:12:56.808
and you cannot outsmart them.
If you befriend the clock,

00:12:56.808 --> 00:12:59.978
the calendar will kill you
in your sleep

00:12:59.978 --> 00:13:01.814
and the clock will laugh.

00:13:01.814 --> 00:13:03.148
[ Laughter ]

00:13:03.148 --> 00:13:07.152
Tick-tock, tick-tock,
that is how a clock laughs.

00:13:07.152 --> 00:13:09.722
A clock is always
laughing at you.

00:13:09.722 --> 00:13:11.056
[ Laughter ]

00:13:11.056 --> 00:13:14.059
So the President
is an adult lunatic

00:13:14.059 --> 00:13:16.929
with a tenuous grasp on reality
propped up by a party

00:13:16.929 --> 00:13:18.330
and a right-wing media apparatus

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:19.799
that lies and rambles
nonsensically.

00:13:19.799 --> 00:13:21.266
In fact, the Republican
contribution

00:13:21.266 --> 00:13:23.768
to the impeachment debate today
was basically a competition

00:13:23.768 --> 00:13:26.405
to see who can be
more sycophantic towards Trump.

00:13:26.405 --> 00:13:27.640
We've already had comparisons

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.508
to the Salem
witch trials and Jesus.

00:13:29.508 --> 00:13:30.475
At then, at one point today,

00:13:30.475 --> 00:13:32.578
a GOP Congressman
literally asked

00:13:32.578 --> 00:13:36.749
for a moment of silence for
the people who voted for Trump.

00:13:36.749 --> 00:13:42.554
-So I want to use my time
to call on this chamber,

00:13:42.554 --> 00:13:49.995
for members to rise and observe
a moment of silent reflection.

00:13:49.995 --> 00:13:55.634
To give every member here
the chance to pause for a moment

00:13:55.634 --> 00:14:01.473
and remember the voices of
the 63 million American voters

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:06.845
the Democrats today
are wanting to silence.

00:14:06.845 --> 00:14:08.914
-Alright.
If the 63 million who voted

00:14:08.914 --> 00:14:10.415
for Trump
get a moment of silence,

00:14:10.415 --> 00:14:12.717
can we also have a moment
for the 66 million

00:14:12.717 --> 00:14:16.655
who voted against him to go,
whaaaaat the [bleep]?

00:14:16.655 --> 00:14:18.757
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:18.757 --> 00:14:21.493
What?

00:14:21.493 --> 00:14:23.295
Among the many important
takeaways today,

00:14:23.295 --> 00:14:24.596
there's one very simple one
that everyone

00:14:24.596 --> 00:14:25.864
should remember
and it's this.

00:14:25.864 --> 00:14:27.265
Impeachment is very popular
and Donald Trump is not.

00:14:27.265 --> 00:14:30.001
Consistently in poll after poll,
about half of Americans

00:14:30.001 --> 00:14:31.971
say Trump should be impeached
and removed from office.

00:14:31.971 --> 00:14:34.439
Even a Fox News poll
found this week

00:14:34.439 --> 00:14:36.909
that 54% of Americans
wanted Trump impeached.

00:14:36.909 --> 00:14:38.644
And that's Fox News,
Trump's favorite channel.

00:14:38.644 --> 00:14:40.679
That would be like
if the Game Show Network

00:14:40.679 --> 00:14:42.781
changed their slogan
to "Okay, boomer."

00:14:42.781 --> 00:14:43.982
[ Laughter ]

00:14:43.982 --> 00:14:46.251
What all of this
comes down to is pretty simple.

00:14:46.251 --> 00:14:48.353
Republicans believe that if
you challenge their power,

00:14:48.353 --> 00:14:50.588
you are illegitimate.
That's why they gerrymander,

00:14:50.588 --> 00:14:53.391
stack the courts, suppress votes
and cheat in elections.

00:14:53.391 --> 00:14:54.726
And that's why impeachment
was necessary

00:14:54.726 --> 00:14:56.328
because we live
in a democracy

00:14:56.328 --> 00:14:59.064
and Trump tried to corrupt
that democracy by cheating,

00:14:59.064 --> 00:15:01.299
and now, he's the third
President ever to be impeached.

00:15:01.299 --> 00:15:02.534
History
will remember this day

00:15:02.534 --> 00:15:04.636
because if you learn
anything from Republicans,

00:15:04.636 --> 00:15:07.205
it's that Trump will not be
able to run away from --

00:15:07.205 --> 00:15:08.406
-The clock and the calendar.
[ Laughter ]

00:15:08.406 --> 00:15:10.709
-This has been "A Closer Look."

